 note: '<strong>The inverter setting scope is complete</strong>. All 23 stations are set, anchored and welded, and on Aug 4 AB Power finished the corrective works on every one of them. That is step 3 of the five that make a station usable plant, so the ladder credits 11.50 station-equivalents, 50.0%. <strong>the gate measure is stations fully terminated and that number is still zero</strong> of 23, with Mechanical Completion on Sep 25. Terminations are gated by the LV/DC pull, which has placed 881 lf of 274,720. Setting went 5 to 13 to 18 to 23 in five days; not one termination has started. Aug 5 added nothing here - AB Power was on substation grounding trenches.',
 dataToConfirm: 'Setting is closed at 23 of 23, so the earlier 17-vs-18 discrepancy is resolved by completion. <strong>the next measure is terminations</strong> and no reporting line exists for it yet - agree with Axel how terminated stations will be counted and reported before the first one is done. Confirm with Axel Cano how many of them are physically on site: each one that is staged rather than merely founded adds 5 points of a station-equivalent. The Jul 12 count of 18 staged is stale and must not be reused.'
